==German==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|de|Kümmel|Türke|t1=caraway|t2=Turk}}. The term was first coined in the 18th century to refer to students from {{m|de|Kümmeltürkei}}, an area so named for its caraway production, but in modern times is used exclusively in a transferred sense as a slur, sometimes explained as being due to Turks smelling like [[caraway]] or [[cumin]].

